            <ArticleTitle>[RESEARCH PROGRESS OF GENDER-SPECIFIC PROSTHESIS].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>693-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To summarize the research progress of the design and effectiveness of gender-specific prosthesis in total knee arthroplasty (TKA).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The relevant literature on gender-specific prosthesis in recent years was extensively reviewed and analyzed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Gender-specific prosthesis is designed according to the female knee joint anatomical characteristics. In theory, it should obtain better effectiveness. But a large number of clinical studies have shown that the knee function, pain, and satisfaction has no obvious advantage when compared with conventional prosthesis after TKA for female patient.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Comprehensive evaluation should be considered when gender-specific is selected; and the effectiveness needs further follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
